  "title": "failure_kind: a gate_red hold is never quota; strip test ids before quota-marker matching",
  "spec": "Why: failures.py:128-129 matches \"cooling\", \"usage limit\", \"quota\", \"rate limit\" as substrings of hold_reason plus all failure text. On 2026-09-30 T-1399 went gate_red on six missing acceptance tests, one named ..._cooling_account, so failure_kind returned quota and the daemon filed no fix round (gotchas.md 2026-09-30).\nWhat: in failure_kind, (1) when hold_reason is gate_red, skip the quota branch entirely; (2) otherwise remove test-id tokens (anything matching the acceptance id pattern path.py::name and pytest node ids) from the text before matching quota markers, and match markers with word boundaries. Keep every other classification unchanged.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused acceptance test in the foreground (uv run python -m pytest <id> -q). Never background a command and never run the full gate; the daemon gates externally. Acceptance ids are tests/<file>.py::<function or method name>; write the test as a unittest.TestCase method using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
